<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ SCRIPT -->
<script is:inline>
  const TRACKS = [
    {
      id: 1,
      title: "Pox Upon You All",
      file: "/audio/pox-album/pox-upon-you-all.mp3",
      slug: "pox-upon-you-all",
      style: "Victorian Music Hall, 120 BPM \u2014 honky-tonk piano, tuba, brass",
      about: "Full Victorian music hall production. Honky-tonk piano, oom-pah tuba, muted brass, and a pompous baritone losing his composure in a smoky gentlemen's club. A female mezzo-soprano arrives to challenge the speaker. Total expressive collapse by the outro.",
      lyrics: `<em>(Jaunty upright piano, breathy tuba oom-pah, crisp snare \u2014 the curtain rises)</em>

<strong>[Verse 1 \u2014 pompous, dignified fury]</strong>
From the very moment I lay eyes upon you \u2014 pox upon the lot of you.
A curse upon what you occupy yourself with, blast what you have suffered,
The devil take where you are bound, a murrain on those who fear you.
Hang you if you served at Her Majesty's pleasure,
Fie upon your coterie, fie upon your quarter \u2014 perdition take your entire rabble!
A plague upon whom you drew your pistol \u2014 rot YOU, and rot your strumpet.
A curse upon you if you've been abroad, deuce take your fraudulent countenance!
A curse upon your life, a curse upon your common drudgery, you miserable wretch \u2014
I care not for you, I care not for your parish,
I care not who you know, I care not if you distribute charity,
I care not who observes \u2014 blast your balderdash!
Blast your shadows, blast whence you came,
A murrain on how you acquired it, rot your entire wretched circumstance!
Hang your pamphlet, hang your scheme,
Perdition take your associates, I care not for your station, you blackguard!
I care not for your grievances, I care not for your conventions!
I care not what manner of counterfeit scoundrel you are!
A curse upon how you conducted your affairs \u2014
I care not who you purport to be!
Rot you if you desire it, rot you if you are villainous,
A plague on you if you parade your finery,
And pox upon these harlots present \u2014 should they not be forthcoming!

<strong>[Interlude \u2014 a woman's voice, sharp and indignant]</strong>
<em>Who in blazes are you calling a harlot, you insufferable wretch?
It appears all the harlots here are harlots \u2014 well I trust you are not addressing me, sir!</em>

<strong>[Chorus \u2014 maximum volume and outrage]</strong>
Blast you! Blast you! Blast the lot of you!
Perdition seize you! The devil take every last one!

<strong>[Verse 2 \u2014 rapid-fire insults, trading with female voice]</strong>
And be damned to you, sir! Be damned!
<em>(Fie upon you, you pompous wretch! Fie!)</em>
Hang you! Hang you! Hang you!
<em>(Rot in perdition! Rot!)</em>

<strong>[Outro \u2014 total expressive collapse, voices shouting over each other]</strong>
Blast you \u2014 be damned \u2014 pox on you \u2014 devil take you \u2014 hang you \u2014 fie \u2014 blast \u2014 DAMNATION!

<em>(Thundering piano chord. Tuba blast. Resonant silence.)</em>`
    },
    {
      id: 2,
      title: "Confound",
      file: "/audio/bonus/confound.mp3",
      slug: "confound",
      style: "Victorian parlour overture, 88 BPM \u2014 string quartet, harpsichord, mezzo interjection",
      about: "Jaunty parlour overture that darkens the instant the speaker opens his mouth. Accelerates through a piled-on tirade, drops to a sparse oom-pah for a dialogue exchange with an outraged mezzo, then collapses into a music-hall brawl.",
      lyrics: `<em>(A jaunty parlour overture. Bows poised. The Gentleman clears his throat.)</em>

<strong>[Verse 1 \u2014 dignified, darkening]</strong>
The next time I clap eyes upon you, I shall say it from the very start:
confound the lot of you.
Confound what you are in pursuit of.
Confound what you have endured.
Confound where you are bound.
Confound whoever is frightened of you.
Confound any time you have served in gaol.

<strong>[Verse 2 \u2014 accelerating]</strong>
Confound your clique. Confound your quarter.
Indeed, confound your whole set.
Confound the person you drew your pistol upon.
Confound you. Confound your mistress.
Confound your being out of town.
Confound that counterfeit icy glower upon your face.

<strong>[Verse 3 \u2014 faster, pressing]</strong>
Confound your life.
Confound your wretched daily drudgery, sir.
I care not one farthing for you.
I care not one farthing for your quarter.
I care not whom you know.
I care not whether you scatter charity.
I care not who is watching.
Confound your balderdash.
Confound your shadows. Confound the place from which you came.
Confound how you obtained it.
Confound your entire situation.

<strong>[Bridge \u2014 rapid-fire]</strong>
Confound your album. Confound your scheme.
Confound your fellows. Confound your part, sir.
I care not one farthing. Confound your brief. Confound your rules.
I care not what manner of false, craven rascal you pretend to be.
Confound the manner in which you ran matters.
I care not whether you call yourself easy.
I care not who you are.
Confound you if you want it.
Confound you if you are sordid.
Confound you if you flaunt your finery.

<strong>[Outro \u2014 deliberate, then dialogue and collapse]</strong>
And confound these women here as well,
if they are not forthcoming.

<em>(A mezzo-soprano interrupts. Voices rise. The quartet scatters into brawl.)</em>`
    },
    {
      id: 3,
      title: "I Care Not For You",
      file: "/audio/bonus/i-care-not-for-you.mp3",
      slug: "i-care-not-for-you",
      style: "Victorian chamber piece, 70 BPM \u2014 string quartet, harpsichord, baritone, two mezzo-sopranos",
      about: "Polite recitative over a mocking minuet, tightening through the first two minutes into breathless agitato. A full stop on one dissonant chord, then a slow grave insult. Two mezzos object, voices overlap, the quartet fractures, glass breaks, one final violin shriek. Curtain.",
      lyrics: `<em>(A mocking minuet. The Gentleman speaks, measured.)</em>

<strong>[Verse 1 \u2014 measured, spoken]</strong>
Upon our reacquaintance, sir, I shall be plain:
I care not for you. I care not for you.
Not for your enthusiasms, not your trials sustained,
Not the harbour where you mean to remain.

<strong>[Verse 2 \u2014 a shade quicker]</strong>
The gentleman who trembles at your tread \u2014 I care not.
Your turn at Her Majesty's pleasure \u2014 I care not.
Your fellowship, your parish, the confederacy you've got,
The men upon whom you have drawn \u2014 I care not.

<strong>[Verse 3 \u2014 quicker, pressing]</strong>
Your person and your lady \u2014 I care not for you.
The Continent you travelled \u2014 I care not for you.
That counterfeit cold scowl, the gilt between your teeth \u2014
I care not for you. I care not for you.

<strong>[Verse 4 \u2014 faster, colour rising]</strong>
Hang your existence, hang your honest trade.
Hang the parish and the acquaintance you have made.
Hang the alms you scatter. Hang the eyes upon your back.
Hang the forked lies on your tongue \u2014 I care not.

<strong>[Bridge \u2014 rapid-fire, breathless]</strong>
Your shadowy confederates, the soil from which you came,
The manner of your fortune, the whole wretched frame,
Your forthcoming publication, your designs, your crew,
The part you fancy you play, the house rules you hold true,
I'll not be acquainted, sir, with you,
You fraudulent dandified wretch \u2014 damn it, damn it, damn it \u2014

<strong>[Break \u2014 one held dissonant chord, then silence]</strong>

<strong>[Verse 5 \u2014 slowly, gravely, deliberate]</strong>
And a pox upon these harlots here present \u2014
if they are not, at this very moment,
engaged in the act of fornication.

<strong>[Exchange \u2014 mezzo-soprano interjects, offended]</strong>
<em>You wretch! Who are you, sir, to call us harlots?</em>
I address every harlot in the room, you hussy.
<em>Whom do you name a hussy?</em>
Every hussy. Every harlot. The lot of you, here, now \u2014

<strong>[Outro \u2014 riot, strings scrape to chaos]</strong>
Scoundrel! The constables! Scoundrel!
<em>(A chair topples. Glass. A final violin shriek.)</em>
Curtain.`
    }
  ];

  // ── DOM refs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  const audio = new Audio();
  audio.preload = 'metadata';
  let currentIndex = -1;
  let isPlaying = false;
  let userInteracted = false;

  const trackListEl = document.getElementById('trackList');
  const npTitle = document.getElementById('npTitle');
  const npBadge = document.getElementById('npBadge');
  const npStyle = document.getElementById('npStyle');
  const npAbout = document.getElementById('npAbout');
  const npLyrics = document.getElementById('npLyrics');
  const playerName = document.getElementById('playerName');
  const playPauseBtn = document.getElementById('playPauseBtn');
  const prevBtn = document.getElementById('prevBtn');
  const nextBtn = document.getElementById('nextBtn');
  const progressBar = document.getElementById('progressBar');
  const curTime = document.getElementById('curTime');
  const durTime = document.getElementById('durTime');
  const volBar = document.getElementById('volBar');
  const playAllBtn = document.getElementById('playAllBtn');

  // ── Build playlist ───────────────────────────────────────────────
  TRACKS.forEach((t, i) => {
    const item = document.createElement('div');
    item.className = 'lr-track-item';
    item.dataset.idx = i;
    item.innerHTML = `
      <span class="lr-track-num">${i + 1}</span>
      <div class="lr-track-info">
        <div class="lr-track-name">${t.title}</div>
        <div class="lr-track-tag">${t.style}</div>
      </div>`;
    item.addEventListener('click', () => loadAndPlay(i));
    trackListEl.appendChild(item);
  });

  // ── Load and play ────────────────────────────────────────────────
  function loadAndPlay(idx) {
    if (idx < 0 || idx >= TRACKS.length) return;
    currentIndex = idx;
    const track = TRACKS[idx];
    audio.src = track.file;
    audio.load();
    audio.play().then(() => { isPlaying = true; updatePlayBtn(); })
      .catch(() => { isPlaying = false; updatePlayBtn(); });
    updateNowPlaying(track, idx);
    updateActiveTrack(idx);
    history.replaceState(null, '', '#' + track.slug);
  }

  function updateNowPlaying(track, idx) {
    npTitle.textContent = track.title;
    npBadge.textContent = `TRACK ${idx + 1}`;
    npStyle.textContent = track.style;
    npAbout.textContent = track.about;
    npLyrics.innerHTML = track.lyrics;
    playerName.textContent = track.title;
  }

  function updateActiveTrack(idx) {
    document.querySelectorAll('.lr-track-item').forEach(el => {
      el.classList.toggle('active', parseInt(el.dataset.idx) === idx);
    });
  }

  function togglePlay() {
    if (currentIndex < 0) { loadAndPlay(0); return; }
    if (isPlaying) { audio.pause(); isPlaying = false; }
    else { audio.play().catch(() => {}); isPlaying = true; }
    updatePlayBtn();
  }

  function updatePlayBtn() {
    if (playPauseBtn) playPauseBtn.textContent = isPlaying ? '\u23F8' : '\u25B6';
  }

  function playPrev() { if (currentIndex > 0) loadAndPlay(currentIndex - 1); }
  function playNext() { if (currentIndex < TRACKS.length - 1) loadAndPlay(currentIndex + 1); }

  function fmt(s) {
    if (!isFinite(s) || isNaN(s)) return '0:00';
    return Math.floor(s / 60) + ':' + String(Math.floor(s % 60)).padStart(2, '0');
  }

  // ── Audio events ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  audio.addEventListener('timeupdate', () => {
    if (!audio.duration) return;
    progressBar.value = (audio.currentTime / audio.duration) * 100;
    curTime.textContent = fmt(audio.currentTime);
  });
  audio.addEventListener('loadedmetadata', () => {
    durTime.textContent = fmt(audio.duration);
    progressBar.value = 0;
  });
  audio.addEventListener('ended', () => { isPlaying = false; updatePlayBtn(); playNext(); });
  audio.addEventListener('play', () => { isPlaying = true; updatePlayBtn(); });
  audio.addEventListener('pause', () => { isPlaying = false; updatePlayBtn(); });

  progressBar.addEventListener('input', () => {
    if (audio.duration) audio.currentTime = (progressBar.value / 100) * audio.duration;
  });
  volBar.addEventListener('input', () => { audio.volume = parseFloat(volBar.value); });

  playPauseBtn.addEventListener('click', togglePlay);
  prevBtn.addEventListener('click', playPrev);
  nextBtn.addEventListener('click', playNext);
  playAllBtn.addEventListener('click', () => loadAndPlay(0));

  // ── Auto-play on load (with hash anchor support) ─────────���───────
  function autoStart() {
    const slug = location.hash.slice(1);
    const hashIdx = slug ? TRACKS.findIndex(t => t.slug === slug) : -1;
    const startIdx = hashIdx >= 0 ? hashIdx : 0;

    updateNowPlaying(TRACKS[startIdx], startIdx);
    updateActiveTrack(startIdx);
    currentIndex = startIdx;
    audio.src = TRACKS[startIdx].file;
    audio.load();
    audio.play().then(() => { isPlaying = true; userInteracted = true; updatePlayBtn(); })
      .catch(() => {
        isPlaying = false;
        updatePlayBtn();
        const resume = () => {
          if (!userInteracted) {
            userInteracted = true;
            audio.play().then(() => { isPlaying = true; updatePlayBtn(); }).catch(() => {});
          }
          document.removeEventListener('click', resume);
          document.removeEventListener('keydown', resume);
        };
        document.addEventListener('click', resume, { once: true });
        document.addEventListener('keydown', resume, { once: true });
      });
  }
  autoStart();
</script>
